# Hardy Hub UI quality

The full rule book is `AGENTS.md` at the repo root. Read it before changing any screen. This file is the short version, and `AGENTS.md` wins if they differ.

The reference page is the Business Setup Modeller (`src/pages/BusinessModeller.tsx` and `src/pages/BusinessModellerDetail.tsx`).

## Never

- Pill shapes. No `rounded-full` on buttons, chips, tabs, filters, badges or toggles. Only avatars, dots, switch thumbs and progress bars are round.
- Pale on pale. No screens built from white cards with faint tints, `bg-muted/40` wells and `text-muted-foreground` everywhere.
- Hover lift (`hover:-translate-y`) as the interaction, soft glows, or gradient icon tiles with a glow.
- Dashed placeholder boxes, "coming soon" shells, or text links standing in for buttons.
- Sideways scrolling pages or control rows, or a small widget that scrolls to reach more buttons.
- Hyphens or dashes joining sentences in any text a person reads.

## Always

- Premium, not loud. Deep jewel tones from `src/lib/brandPalette.ts`, never bright primaries. Serif `font-display` for titles and key figures. Header bands take the `band` class (brass hairline). Cards use a fine 1px border with `shadow-card`.

- Use `Button` from `src/components/ui/button.tsx`, icon first then label. It adds the icon chip and the tactile pressed edge. Do not restyle it per page.
- Solid, saturated colour blocks for section headers, selected options, key numbers and statuses, with white text. Give each section of a page its own strong colour through a `--sec` CSS variable.
- Squared corners from the shared scale: `rounded-md` chips, `rounded-lg` buttons and inputs, `rounded-xl` cards. No `rounded-[...]`.
- Visible borders (`border border-foreground/20` or stronger) and contrast you can see at a glance.
- Pages in `FeaturePageShell`. Section cards with a solid header band. Stat blocks for key numbers.
- Fit all items of a small widget in view by measuring and sizing in pixels (`src/lib/quickLinkGrid.ts`).
- Phone first at 390px. A restyle changes classes and markup only, never logic.
